Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["LPIPS from Wolfram Language via a Python bridge", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"ab796705-0dd7-4674-ab22-214c968e96a2"],

Cell["\<\
This notebook version uses a dedicated Python module, a persistent Python \
session, and thin Wolfram Language wrappers. \
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f22958c3-593d-487f-b0a4-41fc97a1837f"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["1. Python bridge module", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"54b01225-edea-4b11-9c5d-3cdd08074aa7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Save this as ",
 Cell[BoxData[Cell["lpips_bridge.py",
   Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"6a10b65c-0780-4dc1-8d0b-218eba739bc3"]], 
  "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->"e1d648ce-1286-4299-940d-1d06e5ffc7ae"],
 " in the same directory as the notebook. "
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4eeb7b2a-6625-4f15-8845-7db935b0f04c"],

Cell["\<\
from pathlib import Path

import lpips
import numpy as np
import torch
from PIL import Image

_loss_fn_cache = {}


def get_loss_fn(net=\"alex\", version=\"0.1\", spatial=False):
    key = (net, version, spatial)
    if key not in _loss_fn_cache:
        _loss_fn_cache[key] = lpips.LPIPS(net=net, version=version, \
spatial=spatial)
    return _loss_fn_cache[key]


def load_image_tensor(path):
    img = Image.open(path).convert(\"RGB\")
    arr = np.asarray(img).astype(np.float32) / 255.0
    arr = arr * 2.0 - 1.0
    arr = np.transpose(arr, (2, 0, 1))
    return torch.tensor(arr).unsqueeze(0)


def tensor_from_hwc_rgb01(array):
    arr = np.asarray(array, dtype=np.float32)
    arr = arr * 2.0 - 1.0
    arr = np.transpose(arr, (2, 0, 1))
    return torch.tensor(arr).unsqueeze(0)


def lpips_distance(path1, path2, net=\"alex\", version=\"0.1\", spatial=False):
    loss_fn = get_loss_fn(net=net, version=version, spatial=spatial)
    img1 = load_image_tensor(path1)
    img2 = load_image_tensor(path2)
    with torch.no_grad():
        value = loss_fn(img1, img2)
    return float(value.item())


def lpips_distance_batch(pairs, net=\"alex\", version=\"0.1\", \
spatial=False):
    loss_fn = get_loss_fn(net=net, version=version, spatial=spatial)
    results = []
    with torch.no_grad():
        for path1, path2 in pairs:
            img1 = load_image_tensor(path1)
            img2 = load_image_tensor(path2)
            value = loss_fn(img1, img2)
            results.append(float(value.item()))
    return results


def lpips_distance_array(arr1, arr2, net=\"alex\", version=\"0.1\", \
spatial=False):
    loss_fn = get_loss_fn(net=net, version=version, spatial=spatial)
    img1 = tensor_from_hwc_rgb01(arr1)
    img2 = tensor_from_hwc_rgb01(arr2)
\
\>", "ExternalLanguage",
 CellEvaluationLanguage->"Python",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.995974746023559*^9, 
  3.9959747476870317`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e31ff7da-c935-40f3-9e86-\
15b0394a00d2"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["shouldn't the above have 'get_device' embedded too?", "ChatInput",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.995974750992285*^9, 3.995974762264821*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[45]:=",ExpressionUUID->"197bc7ac-02a0-4431-b522-9e2e23024790"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Yes\[LongDash]if you want this bridge to be robust and efficient, it should \
usually include device selection logic such as a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell["get_device[]", Background -> None]},
   "ChatCodeInlineTemplate"]], "ChatCodeActive",ExpressionUUID->
  "94149dc4-9cbe-43f0-8e39-f3eb02b9b152"],
 " equivalent on the Python side.\n\nRight now your module: \n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "caches the LPIPS model in ",
  Cell[BoxData[
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell["_loss_fn_cache", Background -> None]},
    "ChatCodeInlineTemplate"]], "ChatCodeActive",ExpressionUUID->
   "4a66cffe-c908-4bf7-9ba8-67f4cb607594"]
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"71ce00d3-42c1-4389-9434-4d05aa33aa5a"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "loads tensors on the default device"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"e7635232-14a7-488c-829a-ac8ef382bb77"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "never explicitly moves the model or tensors to CPU/GPU"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"97ab7b02-9fd2-42f3-b7fa-b65ea10d0890"],
 "\nThat means it will generally run on CPU unless LPIPS internally does \
something unusual. If you want GPU acceleration, or just predictable \
behavior, adding device management is a good idea. \n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  PaneBox[
   StyleBox["\<\"Why add it?\"\>", "Section",
    CellFrame->0,
    ShowStringCharacters->False,
    FontSize->22],
   ImageMargins->{{0, 0}, {5, 15}}]], "InlineSection",
  Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"ae2dbc39-93f9-4235-8c1b-fc92ae9d4f4c"],
 "\nBecause LPIPS uses PyTorch, and PyTorch models/tensors should live on the \
same device: \n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "model on CPU + tensor on GPU = error"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"ac8f5775-5d6a-4e7b-87cc-2e3c0c53ab35"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "model on GPU + tensor on CPU = error"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"c4a6ee33-f426-4b65-b0be-8f97b6caf952"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "explicit device handling avoids ambiguity"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"a4bc01b2-1742-455f-8809-80f77d3aef16"],
 "\nIt also lets you: \n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "prefer CUDA when available"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"84db2d68-fec7-4214-ad6a-c682457bd3ab"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "fall back to MPS on Apple Silicon if desired"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"2de549fe-49cd-4d67-9bdb-747bbfb4d4c0"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "otherwise use CPU"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"ad13ba62-ce06-410d-a772-4980ad717201"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "cache separate models per device"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"d8137100-6976-4e57-b96c-5816693c2172"],
 "\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  PaneBox[
   StyleBox["\<\"Suggested design\"\>", "Section",
    CellFrame->0,
    ShowStringCharacters->False,
    FontSize->22],
   ImageMargins->{{0, 0}, {5, 15}}]], "InlineSection",
  Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"91ff0333-b771-4621-ae44-0e871e9feeca"],
 "\nAdd: \n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "a ",
  Cell[BoxData[
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell["get_device", Background -> None]},
    "ChatCodeInlineTemplate"]], "ChatCodeActive",ExpressionUUID->
   "ddbc040c-2666-4219-804a-7e18a54b8048"],
  " function"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"7e368d35-ccbd-4fa1-8cf3-c9e8a1801075"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "an optional ",
  StyleBox["device", "TI"],
  " argument to the public functions"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"a2afe7f8-bba9-40d1-b926-59afb8124c04"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "move both the cached LPIPS model and image tensors onto that device"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"0991dfdd-1c91-45bb-9c60-681d7c8bddf7"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "include device in the cache key"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"882c5f58-2744-493a-acd6-b7a1acc929e7"],
 "\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  PaneBox[
   StyleBox["\<\"Example revised module\"\>", "Section",
    CellFrame->0,
    ShowStringCharacters->False,
    FontSize->22],
   ImageMargins->{{0, 0}, {5, 15}}]], "InlineSection",
  Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"b742148a-6889-447f-925b-93d0018a1383"],
 "\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     BoxData[
      Cell[
      "from pathlib import Path\n\nimport lpips\nimport numpy as np\nimport \
torch\nfrom PIL import Image\n\n_loss_fn_cache = {}\n\ndef \
get_device(device=None):\n    if device is not None:\n        return \
torch.device(device)\n    if torch.cuda.is_available():\n        return \
torch.device(\"cuda\")\n    if hasattr(torch.backends, \"mps\") and \
torch.backends.mps.is_available():\n        return torch.device(\"mps\")\n    \
return torch.device(\"cpu\")\n\ndef get_loss_fn(net=\"alex\", \
version=\"0.1\", spatial=False, device=None):\n    dev = \
str(get_device(device))\n    key = (net, version, spatial, dev)\n    if key \
not in _loss_fn_cache:\n        model = lpips.LPIPS(net=net, version=version, \
spatial=spatial)\n        model = model.to(dev)\n        model.eval()\n       \
 _loss_fn_cache[key] = model\n    return _loss_fn_cache[key]\n\ndef \
load_image_tensor(path, device=None):\n    img = \
Image.open(path).convert(\"RGB\")\n    arr = \
np.asarray(img).astype(np.float32) / 255.0\n    arr = arr * 2.0 - 1.0\n    \
arr = np.transpose(arr, (2, 0, 1))\n    return \
torch.tensor(arr).unsqueeze(0).to(get_device(device))\n\ndef \
tensor_from_hwc_rgb01(array, device=None):\n    arr = np.asarray(array, \
dtype=np.float32)\n    arr = arr * 2.0 - 1.0\n    arr = np.transpose(arr, (2, \
0, 1))\n    return torch.tensor(arr).unsqueeze(0).to(get_device(device))\n\n\
def lpips_distance(path1, path2, net=\"alex\", version=\"0.1\", \
spatial=False, device=None):\n    loss_fn = get_loss_fn(net=net, \
version=version, spatial=spatial, device=device)\n    img1 = \
load_image_tensor(path1, device=device)\n    img2 = load_image_tensor(path2, \
device=device)\n    with torch.no_grad():\n        value = loss_fn(img1, \
img2)\n    return float(value.item())\n\ndef lpips_distance_batch(pairs, net=\
\"alex\", version=\"0.1\", spatial=False, device=None):\n    loss_fn = \
get_loss_fn(net=net, version=version, spatial=spatial, device=device)\n    \
results = []\n    with torch.no_grad():\n        for path1, path2 in pairs:\n \
           img1 = load_image_tensor(path1, device=device)\n            img2 = \
load_image_tensor(path2, device=device)\n            value = loss_fn(img1, \
img2)\n            results.append(float(value.item()))\n    return results\n\n\
def lpips_distance_array(arr1, arr2, net=\"alex\", version=\"0.1\", \
spatial=False, device=None):\n    loss_fn = get_loss_fn(net=net, \
version=version, spatial=spatial, device=device)\n    img1 = \
tensor_from_hwc_rgb01(arr1, device=device)\n    img2 = \
tensor_from_hwc_rgb01(arr2, device=device)\n    with torch.no_grad():\n       \
 value = loss_fn(img1, img2)\n    return float(value.item())", 
       "ExternalLanguage", CellEvaluationLanguage -> "Python", FontSize -> 13,
        Background -> None, CellFrame -> None]]], "Python"},
   "ChatCodeBlockTemplate"]], "ChatCodeBlock",ExpressionUUID->
  "7b53db2e-a770-4c2c-9f79-91419e1bcb51"],
 "\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  PaneBox[
   StyleBox["\<\"A couple of notes\"\>", "Section",
    CellFrame->0,
    ShowStringCharacters->False,
    FontSize->22],
   ImageMargins->{{0, 0}, {5, 15}}]], "InlineSection",
  Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"ee2f5765-2fb7-45e5-81ce-d56d7fbd2edd"],
 "\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  PaneBox[
   StyleBox["\<\"1. Your posted module is incomplete\"\>", "Subsection",
    CellFrame->0,
    ShowStringCharacters->False],
   ImageMargins->{{0, 0}, {5, 15}}]], "InlineSection",
  Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"68fa18c0-c751-4464-bf48-bb334fa54ba2"],
 "\nThe function ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell["lpips_distance_array", Background -> None]},
   "ChatCodeInlineTemplate"]], "ChatCodeActive",ExpressionUUID->
  "db1b03b7-fa28-4893-be47-1a392c5bf83d"],
 " in your snippet stops after: \n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     BoxData[
      Cell[
      "img2 = tensor_from_hwc_rgb01(arr2)", "ExternalLanguage", 
       CellEvaluationLanguage -> "Python", FontSize -> 13, Background -> None,
        CellFrame -> None]]], "Python"},
   "ChatCodeBlockTemplate"]], "ChatCodeBlock",ExpressionUUID->
  "0abd04ca-2f19-4533-820d-f95795028638"],
 "\nIt still needs the actual LPIPS call and return. \n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  PaneBox[
   StyleBox["\<\"2. Cache key should include device\"\>", "Subsection",
    CellFrame->0,
    ShowStringCharacters->False],
   ImageMargins->{{0, 0}, {5, 15}}]], "InlineSection",
  Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"ff244007-e2bf-4de0-a304-44014533c67a"],
 "\nIf you cache only by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell["(net, version, spatial)", Background -> None]},
   "ChatCodeInlineTemplate"]], "ChatCodeActive",ExpressionUUID->
  "72022d19-4fbe-4bab-97c1-266e089398d2"],
 ", then the first-created model might stay on CPU and later GPU requests \
would reuse the wrong model. Including device in the key fixes that. \n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  PaneBox[
   StyleBox[Cell[TextData[{
     "3. ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      TemplateBox[{
        Cell["model.eval()", Background -> None]},
       "ChatCodeInlineTemplate"]], "ChatCodeActive",ExpressionUUID->
      "951d1746-8db9-4d03-a5d4-853df562ab00"],
     " is a good idea"
    }],
     Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"029de59c-126e-4678-8b2c-682f93240f8f"],
     "Subsection",
    CellFrame->0,
    ShowStringCharacters->False],
   ImageMargins->{{0, 0}, {5, 15}}]], "InlineSection",
  Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"eb5a2ad6-3477-4cb2-a66d-3d36b3e2efe6"],
 "\nLPIPS is inference-only here, so calling ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell["eval()", Background -> None]},
   "ChatCodeInlineTemplate"]], "ChatCodeActive",ExpressionUUID->
  "3e15df9b-c4da-4527-8af7-2facbebdf421"],
 " is appropriate and makes behavior explicit. \n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  PaneBox[
   StyleBox["\<\"4. Optional explicit device from Wolfram Language\"\>", 
    "Subsection",
    CellFrame->0,
    ShowStringCharacters->False],
   ImageMargins->{{0, 0}, {5, 15}}]], "InlineSection",
  Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"ef960fe2-9518-4a3b-b2de-7f0d0acaf9ae"],
 "\nThis is especially useful from the WL side, e.g. passing: \n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  Cell[BoxData["\"\<cpu\>\""], "InlineWL", "Input",
   ShowAutoStyles->True,
   ShowSyntaxStyles->True,
   LanguageCategory->"Input",
   ShowStringCharacters->True,ExpressionUUID->
   "ed09aa08-e060-4cf8-93a3-44763c5c2b2a"]
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"ba0e0b5f-52bb-458e-96f3-291d5840c1ab"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  Cell[BoxData["\"\<cuda\>\""], "InlineWL", "Input",
   ShowAutoStyles->True,
   ShowSyntaxStyles->True,
   LanguageCategory->"Input",
   ShowStringCharacters->True,ExpressionUUID->
   "c156afce-f51e-4e56-82e5-3504b3a1bcba"]
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"a2ca13c7-02dc-4ab9-b3a1-58fb11536468"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  Cell[BoxData["\"\<mps\>\""], "InlineWL", "Input",
   ShowAutoStyles->True,
   ShowSyntaxStyles->True,
   LanguageCategory->"Input",
   ShowStringCharacters->True,ExpressionUUID->
   "0eced2e2-5b26-4424-9e70-900f59307f54"]
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"12bf8e31-d14d-465c-a984-df5042830732"],
 "\nrather than relying only on auto-detection. \n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  PaneBox[
   StyleBox["\<\"Recommendation\"\>", "Section",
    CellFrame->0,
    ShowStringCharacters->False,
    FontSize->22],
   ImageMargins->{{0, 0}, {5, 15}}]], "InlineSection",
  Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"838d1357-4a90-4887-9ece-fa2c3f9c892e"],
 "\nSo: **yes, I would embed ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell["get_device", Background -> None]},
   "ChatCodeInlineTemplate"]], "ChatCodeActive",ExpressionUUID->
  "d657764a-a9e3-4092-95d4-ef8191bdb439"],
 " in the Python bridge**.\n\nThat keeps the bridge self-contained and avoids \
duplicating device policy in the Wolfram Language wrapper layer. The WL \
wrappers can then simply pass through a device string when needed.\n\nIf you \
want, I can also draft the matching thin Wolfram Language wrappers for this \
revised Python module, including a persistent ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
   "ExternalSessionObject", "paclet:ref/ExternalSessionObject", 
    "https://reference.wolfram.com/language/ref/ExternalSessionObject.html"},
   "TextRefLink"]],ExpressionUUID->"bf9a0037-e4b1-42de-9f58-52f0cb907611"],
 " and option handling for ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Device\>\""], "InlineWL", "Input",
  ShowAutoStyles->True,
  ShowSyntaxStyles->True,
  LanguageCategory->"Input",
  ShowStringCharacters->True,ExpressionUUID->
  "0eef964c-e1fa-4ae4-ab61-a08c2f22cb57"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Network\>\""], "InlineWL", "Input",
  ShowAutoStyles->True,
  ShowSyntaxStyles->True,
  LanguageCategory->"Input",
  ShowStringCharacters->True,ExpressionUUID->
  "e9e52e40-037b-41e2-ad87-1e9d64be6bc3"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Version\>\""], "InlineWL", "Input",
  ShowAutoStyles->True,
  ShowSyntaxStyles->True,
  LanguageCategory->"Input",
  ShowStringCharacters->True,ExpressionUUID->
  "d813e84c-f60b-437a-8175-3098fd422742"],
 "."
}], "ChatOutput",
 TaggingRules-><|
  "CellToStringData" -> 
   "Yes\[LongDash]if you want this bridge to be robust and efficient, it \
should usually include device selection logic such as a ``get_device[]`` \
equivalent on the Python side.\n\nRight now your module:\n\n- caches the \
LPIPS model in ``_loss_fn_cache``\n- loads tensors on the default device\n- \
never explicitly moves the model or tensors to CPU/GPU\n\nThat means it will \
generally run on CPU unless LPIPS internally does something unusual. If you \
want GPU acceleration, or just predictable behavior, adding device management \
is a good idea.\n\n## Why add it?\n\nBecause LPIPS uses PyTorch, and PyTorch \
models/tensors should live on the same device:\n\n- model on CPU + tensor on \
GPU = error\n- model on GPU + tensor on CPU = error\n- explicit device \
handling avoids ambiguity\n\nIt also lets you:\n\n- prefer CUDA when \
available\n- fall back to MPS on Apple Silicon if desired\n- otherwise use \
CPU\n- cache separate models per device\n\n## Suggested design\n\nAdd:\n\n- a \
``get_device`` function\n- an optional ``device`` argument to the public \
functions\n- move both the cached LPIPS model and image tensors onto that \
device\n- include device in the cache key\n\n## Example revised module\n\n\
```python\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport lpips\nimport numpy as np\n\
import torch\nfrom PIL import Image\n\n_loss_fn_cache = {}\n\ndef \
get_device(device=None):\n    if device is not None:\n        return \
torch.device(device)\n    if torch.cuda.is_available():\n        return \
torch.device(\"cuda\")\n    if hasattr(torch.backends, \"mps\") and \
torch.backends.mps.is_available():\n        return torch.device(\"mps\")\n    \
return torch.device(\"cpu\")\n\ndef get_loss_fn(net=\"alex\", \
version=\"0.1\", spatial=False, device=None):\n    dev = \
str(get_device(device))\n    key = (net, version, spatial, dev)\n    if key \
not in _loss_fn_cache:\n        model = lpips.LPIPS(net=net, version=version, \
spatial=spatial)\n        model = model.to(dev)\n        model.eval()\n       \
 _loss_fn_cache[key] = model\n    return _loss_fn_cache[key]\n\ndef \
load_image_tensor(path, device=None):\n    img = \
Image.open(path).convert(\"RGB\")\n    arr = \
np.asarray(img).astype(np.float32) / 255.0\n    arr = arr * 2.0 - 1.0\n    \
arr = np.transpose(arr, (2, 0, 1))\n    return \
torch.tensor(arr).unsqueeze(0).to(get_device(device))\n\ndef \
tensor_from_hwc_rgb01(array, device=None):\n    arr = np.asarray(array, \
dtype=np.float32)\n    arr = arr * 2.0 - 1.0\n    arr = np.transpose(arr, (2, \
0, 1))\n    return torch.tensor(arr).unsqueeze(0).to(get_device(device))\n\n\
def lpips_distance(path1, path2, net=\"alex\", version=\"0.1\", \
spatial=False, device=None):\n    loss_fn = get_loss_fn(net=net, \
version=version, spatial=spatial, device=device)\n    img1 = \
load_image_tensor(path1, device=device)\n    img2 = load_image_tensor(path2, \
device=device)\n    with torch.no_grad():\n        value = loss_fn(img1, \
img2)\n    return float(value.item())\n\ndef lpips_distance_batch(pairs, net=\
\"alex\", version=\"0.1\", spatial=False, device=None):\n    loss_fn = \
get_loss_fn(net=net, version=version, spatial=spatial, device=device)\n    \
results = []\n    with torch.no_grad():\n        for path1, path2 in pairs:\n \
           img1 = load_image_tensor(path1, device=device)\n            img2 = \
load_image_tensor(path2, device=device)\n            value = loss_fn(img1, \
img2)\n            results.append(float(value.item()))\n    return results\n\n\
def lpips_distance_array(arr1, arr2, net=\"alex\", version=\"0.1\", \
spatial=False, device=None):\n    loss_fn = get_loss_fn(net=net, \
version=version, spatial=spatial, device=device)\n    img1 = \
tensor_from_hwc_rgb01(arr1, device=device)\n    img2 = \
tensor_from_hwc_rgb01(arr2, device=device)\n    with torch.no_grad():\n       \
 value = loss_fn(img1, img2)\n    return float(value.item())\n```\n\n## A \
couple of notes\n\n### 1. Your posted module is incomplete\n\nThe function \
``lpips_distance_array`` in your snippet stops after:\n\n```python\nimg2 = \
tensor_from_hwc_rgb01(arr2)\n```\n\nIt still needs the actual LPIPS call and \
return.\n\n### 2. Cache key should include device\n\nIf you cache only by \
``(net, version, spatial)``, then the first-created model might stay on CPU \
and later GPU requests would reuse the wrong model. Including device in the \
key fixes that.\n\n### 3. ``model.eval()`` is a good idea\n\nLPIPS is \
inference-only here, so calling ``eval()`` is appropriate and makes behavior \
explicit.\n\n### 4. Optional explicit device from Wolfram Language\n\nThis is \
especially useful from the WL side, e.g. passing:\n\n- ``\"cpu\"``\n- \
``\"cuda\"``\n- ``\"mps\"``\n\nrather than relying only on auto-detection.\n\n\
## Recommendation\n\nSo: **yes, I would embed ``get_device`` in the Python \
bridge**.\n\nThat keeps the bridge self-contained and avoids duplicating \
device policy in the Wolfram Language wrapper layer. The WL wrappers can then \
simply pass through a device string when needed.\n\nIf you want, I can also \
draft the matching thin Wolfram Language wrappers for this revised Python \
module, including a persistent ``ExternalSessionObject`` and option handling \
for ``\"Device\"``, ``\"Network\"``, and ``\"Version\"``.", "ChatData" -> 
